{#- The same header on every page: the name on the left, the four places you can be,
    and the light switch. It is one file because copies of a navigation bar drift apart —
    they had already drifted into three different orders once.

    The order is how often somebody wants each one. Learn is most visits; Library is
    finding the next thing; Your Progress is deliberate study; Add, bringing a text of
    your own, is the rarest.

    Two things left this row on 2026-09-06 (design.md §12, "The front door is a
    question"). The chat was second here for a day — added 2026-09-05 as where you go
    when you do not know what to pick up — and is now the box at the top of Learn, so
    the conversation page marks Learn the way Learn's own lists do. Uploading a text was
    never a place at all; it sat in the corner with the account, and it is now the `+`
    on that box.

    Add came back on 2026-09-13 (design.md §12, "Add is a place again"): with the box in a
    drawer, the Add page had no door but the card's "More options" and ⌘K. It is last,
    and it is the one place that keeps its glyph at a desk — a `+` before the word, the
    way the product already says "bring something". The `+` on the box stays.

    Your Progress was called Words until it became an account of what a reader has built
    rather than a list of what they had kept. It is the only two-word label here, which
    is why the row wraps rather than scrolls under a narrow window.

    Set `here` to "learn", "chat", "library", "progress" or "add" before including this. -#}
{{ chrome_face() }}
<header class="site-head">
  <div class="site-head-row">
    {#- The lockup, assembled live rather than dropped in as lockup.svg: the name is
        real text in the reading face the page already loads, so it stays selectable and
        scales with the user's type size, and the mark takes its two colours from the
        palette so it turns over with the theme. -#}
    <a class="brand" href="/">
      <svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="20 12 56 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <rect x="20" y="12" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="currentColor"></rect>
        <rect x="54" y="22" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="var(--mark-accent)"></rect>
      </svg>
      <span>targum</span>
    </a>
    <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="{{ t("nav.pages", "Pages") }}">
      {#- On a phone the four places are a bar at the foot of the window, a glyph over
          each word (phase 4, 2026-09-11); at a desk only Add draws its glyph. §7: sixteen
          pixels, a stroke at 1.4, round caps. -#}
      <a href="/" data-nav="learn"{% if here in ('learn', 'chat') %} class="on" aria-current="page"{% endif %}><svg class="nav-glyph" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 3.5h4a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 1.5 1.5v8a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5-1.5h-4zM13.5 3.5h-4A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 8 5v8a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 1.5-1.5h4z"/></svg><span>{{ t("nav.learn", "Learn") }}</span></a>
      <a href="/library" data-nav="library"{% if here == 'library' %} class="on" aria-current="page"{% endif %}><svg class="nav-glyph" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 2.5h2.5v11H2.5zM6.5 2.5H9v11H6.5zM10.2 3.2l2.4-.6 2.6 10.6-2.4.6z"/></svg><span>{{ t("nav.library", "Library") }}</span></a>
      <a href="/progress" data-nav="progress"{% if here == 'progress' %} class="on" aria-current="page"{% endif %}><svg class="nav-glyph" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 13.5h11M3.5 11l3-3.5 2.5 2 3.5-4.5"/></svg><span><span class="nav-your">{{ t("nav.your", "Your") }} </span>{{ t("nav.progress", "Progress") }}</span></a>
      <a href="/add" data-nav="add" class="nav-add{% if here == 'add' %} on{% endif %}"{% if here == 'add' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}><svg class="nav-glyph" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 3.5v9M3.5 8h9"/></svg><span>{{ t("nav.add", "Add") }}</span></a>
    </nav>
    {#- Which language (design.md §13, 2026-09-13): one menu at the end of the places on
        every desk page that reads in a language, filled by `lang.js`. Hidden until the
        reader learns more than one: a menu with one thing in it asks nothing. -#}
    {%- if here in ('learn', 'chat', 'library', 'progress', 'add', 'yours', 'you') %}
    <div class="langs" id="langs" hidden></div>
    {%- endif %}
    {#- Notifications, in the corner of every page (2026-09-11): what is building and
        what is ready, and anything else the page has to say later. The bell carries a
        count; the panel lists them, newest first, each with its own × and Clear all
        above them; the panel stays open while you put lines away. It replaced the
        pill that stood fixed at the foot of the window. Drawn by `building.js`. -#}
    {#- The command palette's own door (2026-09-11), beside the bell; ⌘K is the other. -#}
    <button type="button" class="palette-open" id="palette-open" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="palette" aria-label="{{ t("nav.find-anything", "Find anything") }}" title="{{ t("nav.find-anything-k", "Find anything (⌘K)") }}">
      <svg class="bell" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="7" cy="7" r="4.2"/><path d="M10.2 10.2 13.5 13.5"/></svg>
    </button>
    <div class="notices" id="notices">
      <button type="button" id="notices-open" aria-expanded="false" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="{{ t("nav.notifications", "Notifications") }}">
        <svg class="bell" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 2.2a3.6 3.6 0 0 0-3.6 3.6v2.4L3.2 10.6h9.6l-1.2-2.4V5.8A3.6 3.6 0 0 0 8 2.2zM6.6 12.6a1.4 1.4 0 0 0 2.8 0"/></svg>
        <span class="notices-count" id="notices-count" hidden></span>
      </button>
      <div class="notices-panel" id="notices-panel" role="dialog" aria-label="{{ t("nav.notifications", "Notifications") }}" hidden>
        {#- Clear all (2026-09-14): every line put away at once, as each × would. Shown
            only while there is something to clear. -#}
        <div class="notices-head" id="notices-head" hidden>
          <button type="button" class="notices-clear" id="notices-clear">{{ t("nav.clear-all", "Clear all") }}</button>
        </div>
        <p class="notices-empty" id="notices-empty">{{ t("nav.we-re-not-building-anything-right-now", "We're not building anything right now.") }}</p>
        <ul class="notices-list" id="notices-list"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="account" id="account">
      <button type="button" id="account-open" aria-expanded="false" aria-haspopup="dialog">
        {{ t("nav.sign-in", "Sign in") }}
      </button>
      <div class="account-panel" id="account-panel" role="dialog" aria-label="{{ t("nav.your-account", "Your account") }}" hidden>
        {#- Your Words: the words and phrases you are learning, behind the account since
            2026-09-11 ("a dedicated page you access by clicking on your picture in the
            top right"). Above both halves of the panel: it is yours signed in or not. -#}
        <p class="yours-link"><a class="to-you" href="/words">{{ t("nav.your-words-and-phrases", "Your words and phrases") }}</a>
          <a class="to-you" href="/you#subscriptions">{{ t("nav.your-subscriptions", "Your subscriptions") }}</a></p>
        {#- On a phone the top bar keeps the mark, the language, the bell and the account
            (design.md §13), so find and the light switch are here (2026-09-14). -#}
        <p class="account-phone">
          <button type="button" class="account-find" data-palette-open>{{ t("nav.find-anything", "Find anything") }}</button>
          <span class="account-theme">{{ t("nav.light-or-dark", "Light or dark") }} <button type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-label="{{ t("nav.switch-theme", "Switch theme") }}"></button></span>
        </p>
        <div class="signed-out">
          <p>{{ t("nav.your-words-follow-you-no-password-we", "Your words follow you. No password. We'll email you a link.") }}</p>
          <form id="account-form">
            <input type="email" id="account-email" placeholder="{{ t("nav.you-example-com", "you@example.com") }}"
                   autocomplete="email" spellcheck="false" required>
            <button type="submit">{{ t("nav.send-a-link", "Send a link") }}</button>
          </form>
        </div>
        <div class="signed-in" hidden>
          <p class="whom" id="account-whom"></p>
          {#- The month's hours, in the unit the pricing page gives them: where a reader
              who wonders looks, and nowhere they did not (targum-internal#237). -#}
          <p class="hours" id="account-hours" hidden></p>
          <a class="to-you" href="/you">{{ t("nav.your-profile", "Your profile") }}</a>
          <button type="button" id="account-out">{{ t("nav.sign-out", "Sign out") }}</button>
        </div>
        <p class="said" id="account-said" hidden></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <button type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-label="{{ t("nav.switch-theme", "Switch theme") }}"></button>
  </div>
  {% if title %}<h1>{{ title }}</h1>{% endif %}
  {%- if here in ('learn', 'library', 'progress') %}
  <p class="beta-note" id="beta-note" hidden></p>
  {%- endif %}
</header>
{#- What a reader follows, on every page (2026-09-11): the bell says when a followed
    series' instalment lands, and Learn puts it in the sheet. Before `building.js`, which
    every page includes after this header and which asks it. -#}
<script>{{ asset('follow.js') }}</script>
{#- Talk to targum, from anywhere (2026-09-11): one pill fixed at the foot of every page
    opens the conversation as a drawer — the conversation page framed without its bar.
    Nothing is loaded until it is opened. Drawn by `talk.js`. -#}
<button type="button" class="talk-cta" id="talk-open" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="talk-drawer" aria-label="{{ t("nav.talk-to-targum", "Talk to targum") }}"><svg class="talk-glyph" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 2.5c-3.3 0-6 2.2-6 5 0 1.5.8 2.9 2.1 3.8L3.5 13.5l3-1.3c.5.1 1 .2 1.5.2 3.3 0 6-2.2 6-5s-2.7-4.9-6-4.9z"/></svg><span>{{ t("nav.talk-to-targum", "Talk to targum") }}</span></button>
<div class="talk-scrim" id="talk-scrim" hidden></div>
<aside class="talk-drawer" id="talk-drawer" aria-label="{{ t("nav.talk-to-targum", "Talk to targum") }}" hidden>
  <div class="talk-drawer-head">
    <span class="talk-drawer-title">{{ t("nav.talk-to-targum", "Talk to targum") }}</span>
    <button type="button" class="talk-close" id="talk-close" aria-label="{{ t("nav.close", "Close") }}">×</button>
  </div>
  <iframe class="talk-frame" id="talk-frame" title="{{ t("nav.talk-to-targum", "Talk to targum") }}" allow="microphone" data-src="/chat?embed=1{% if token %}&amp;k={{ token }}{% endif %}"></iframe>
</aside>
<script>{{ asset('talk.js') }}</script>
{#- The command palette (2026-09-11): one field that finds a place, a text, a series or
    a conversation, and one press that goes there. Drawn by `palette.js`. -#}
<div class="palette-scrim" id="palette-scrim" hidden></div>
<div class="palette" id="palette" role="dialog" aria-label="{{ t("nav.find-anything", "Find anything") }}" hidden>
  <input type="search" id="palette-find" class="palette-find" dir="auto" placeholder="{{ t("nav.find-a-text-a-page-a-conversation", "Find a text, a page, a conversation") }}" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
  <ul class="palette-list" id="palette-list" role="listbox"></ul>
</div>
<script>{{ asset('palette.js') }}</script>
